From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 13:30:00 +1000
Subject: media: qcom: iris: Keep the timestamp metadata index in range

iris_set_ts_metadata() wraps inst->metadata_idx before it writes an
entry and increments it afterwards, so after the 32nd input buffer the
index is ARRAY_SIZE(inst->tss) until the next one is queued. When a
capture buffer's timestamp matches no entry, iris_get_ts_metadata()
falls back to inst->tss[inst->metadata_idx] and reads past the array.
That happens for any capture buffer whose timestamp is not among the 32
most recently queued, such as the empty LAST buffer once it is no longer
flagged as an error. Seen on a Radxa Dragon Q6A after seeks:

  UBSAN: array-index-out-of-bounds in iris_buffer.c:869:26
  index 32 is out of range for type 'iris_ts_metadata [32]'

Wrap the index when it is incremented, so it always points at the
oldest entry.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_common.c | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_common.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_common.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_common.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_common.c
@@ -33,9 +33,6 @@
 	struct vb2_buffer *vb = &vbuf->vb2_buf;
 	u64 ts_us = vb->timestamp;
 
-	if (inst->metadata_idx >= ARRAY_SIZE(inst->tss))
-		inst->metadata_idx = 0;
-
 	do_div(ts_us, NSEC_PER_USEC);
 
 	inst->tss[inst->metadata_idx].flags = vbuf->flags & mask;
@@ -43,7 +40,7 @@
 	inst->tss[inst->metadata_idx].ts_us = ts_us;
 	inst->tss[inst->metadata_idx].ts_ns = vb->timestamp;
 
-	inst->metadata_idx++;
+	inst->metadata_idx = (inst->metadata_idx + 1) % ARRAY_SIZE(inst->tss);
 }
 
 int iris_process_streamon_input(struct iris_inst *inst)
